{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/validate-workstreams.py::validate_workstreams_semantics", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [126, 127, 128, 129], "why": "The team member sets (gc_members, tc_members, spec_sponsors) are built from people_data inside the per-workstream loop that starts at line 116, although they depend only on people_data and not on the workstream. They are rebuilt once per workstream."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [103], "why": "`parent_kind` is assigned from id_to_workstream[parent_id] and never read afterwards."}, {"label": "c", "lines": [105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111, 112, 113, 114], "why": "The parent-chain walk for cycle detection starts again from every workstream, so the total work is O(workstreams x chain depth) with no memo of already-checked chains."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/update-sig-tables.py::render_group", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [157], "why": "extract_row_data(ws) is computed here for each SIG, and render_sig_details computes the same dict again for the same SIG in sigs.md. Each SIG's row data is built twice per run."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [159], "why": "The table body is grown with `content +=` once per SIG row. The suspicion is the quadratic cost of repeated string concatenation."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/update-sig-tables.py::render_sig_details", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [166], "why": "extract_row_data(ws) repeats the work render_group already did for the same ws (line 157) during the README pass, so each SIG's row data is built twice per run."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/update-sig-tables.py::heading_anchor", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [50, 51], "why": "Two regex patterns are passed to re.sub as literals on every call, so they are compiled through the re module cache on each call. heading_anchor runs once per SIG."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/gc-elections/create-github-comments.py::sync", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [141, 142, 143, 144, 145, 146, 147, 148], "why": "Stale handles are removed one at a time: remove_handle_line makes a full regex pass over the comment body for each stale handle, so a comment with k stale handles is scanned k times."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [136, 145, 157], "why": "extract_mentions is run over the same comment body three times per comment: once to build tagged_lower, once to find stale handles, and once more on new_body to decide whether the comment is now empty."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/gc-elections/create-github-comments.py::is_voter_comment", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [101], "why": "body.splitlines() builds a list of every line of the whole comment, but only lines[0] is read. A comment with 50 voters is about 50 lines."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/gc-elections/create-github-comments.py::remove_handle_line", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [110, 111, 112, 113], "why": "The handle-specific pattern is built and passed to re.compile on every call, even though it is called once per stale handle per comment and the pattern does not change between comments for the same handle."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/gc-elections/generate-voters-roll.py::get_github_login", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [29], "why": "time.sleep(0.1) runs before every GitHub users API request, so each contributor adds 0.1 s of wall-clock idle time whatever the response was."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [36], "why": "requests.get is called as a bare function with no Session, so each username opens a new TCP connection and a new TLS handshake to api.github.com."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/gc-elections/generate-voters-roll.py::build_devstats_rows", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [93, 94, 95, 96], "why": "get_github_login is called in sequence for every devstats name, so the run makes one blocking HTTP round trip per contributor, and each one is preceded by the 0.1 s sleep."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/baremetal-runner-report.py::collect_jobs", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [83, 92, 93, 94, 95], "why": "The job list is fetched for every completed run in the window, one paginated gh api call per run, and each run's jobs are read in full before the bare-metal label filter at lines 101 to 105 is applied. Runs in workflows whose jobs never carry the label still cost a request each."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/baremetal-runner-report.py::gh_paginated", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [43, 44, 45, 46, 47, 48], "why": "Each call starts a new `gh` process, which pays interpreter-style start-up and authentication before the request is sent. collect_jobs calls it once per run, so the run starts one subprocess per run."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/baremetal-runner-report.py::render_table", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [147, 148, 149], "why": "render_table walks the full records list once per window. main calls it for each of the two windows, so records are filtered twice, once for each window start."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_get_repo_commenters", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [256, 257], "why": "`number not in commenters[user][kind]` is a linear scan of a list each time a comment is read, so the work per user is quadratic in the number of distinct PRs or issues they commented on."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_check_events", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [343, 344, 345, 346, 347, 348, 349], "why": "The loop walks every cached event for the repo even after every user in remaining has already been found, so the rest of the list is scanned for nothing."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_verify_review_candidates", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [358, 359, 360, 361], "why": "The reviews of a candidate PR are fetched again on every call that reaches that PR, so a PR that is a candidate for several users in the same repo is fetched once per user. Nothing caches reviews per (repo, PR)."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_check_reviews", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [455], "why": "Verification runs per user in each batch of ten, so a PR that is a candidate for two users in the batch is verified twice. The candidate lists are not merged or deduplicated across the batch before verification."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::check_triager_activity", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [497, 507, 512], "why": "debug() takes an f-string, so each message, including `_fmt_numbers(numbers)`, is built even when DEBUG is False and debug() prints nothing."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::check_approver_activity", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [541, 550, 559, 566], "why": "debug() is called with eagerly built f-strings (including `_fmt_numbers(numbers)`) even when DEBUG is False."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [539, 548], "why": "_check_comments is called twice per repo, once with comment_type=\"pr\" and once with \"issue\". Both passes read the same cached commenters and rescan the same remaining users."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::check_maintainer_activity", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [597, 606, 615, 650, 662, 667], "why": "debug() is called with eagerly built f-strings even when DEBUG is False. Line 650 also runs `_extract_numbers(authored_result)` for every user with authored PRs, only to format the debug message."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_add_to_emeritus", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [859, 872], "why": "The member-line regex `^[-*+] \\[` is run over the same section lines twice: once to build member_lines (line 859) and again to find the first and last member indices (lines 871 to 875)."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_remove_member_line", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [817], "why": "_find_section scans the whole README for the section header on every call. create_emeritus_prs calls this once per user per role, so the same README is searched many times."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::create_emeritus_prs", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [1198, 1199, 1200, 1201, 1202, 1203, 1204, 1205, 1206, 1207, 1208, 1209, 1210], "why": "For each user and each of their roles, the same README sections are located with _find_section and re-parsed with _parse_members to find a display name, so every README section is parsed once per user rather than once per repo."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [1223, 1224, 1225, 1230], "why": "The README string is rebuilt in full by each _remove_member_line and _add_to_emeritus call, so each user costs several full copies of the README."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_ensure_fork", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [967, 968], "why": "After the fork POST the loop sleeps 5 s before its first check of the fork, so a fork that is already ready still costs at least 5 s of wall-clock idle time."}, {"label": "b", "lines": [982, 983, 984, 985, 989], "why": "The refs endpoint is polled with a fixed 5 s sleep between attempts rather than a shorter backoff, so each wait is at least 5 s."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_create_followup_issue", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [1148, 1149, 1150, 1151, 1152, 1156, 1157, 1158, 1159, 1160], "why": "The whole list of open issues in the repo is paged through, 100 per request, to find one with the matching title, and it is walked again on each run."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_get_emeritus_pr_number", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [721, 722, 723, 724, 725, 726, 727, 728, 729, 730, 731, 732, 733, 734], "why": "All open PRs in the repo are paged through, 100 per request, to find the one with the move-to-emeritus head branch. The head filter is not used, so the walk runs to the last page for any repo without such a PR."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::_find_section", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [768, 769, 770, 771, 780], "why": "Two regex patterns are built from f-strings on every call. They are compiled through the re cache each time, and this runs once per section lookup."}]}
{"step": 1, "unit": "scripts/move-to-emeritus.py::main", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "lines": [1323, 1326, 1327], "why": "get_team_repos fetches every repo of each team before the --repo filter at lines 1326 and 1327 is applied, so a run restricted to one repo still pages through every team's full repo list."}]}

